Z||000003||Slammed Fiero||01-29-2001||03:39 PM||||Good question<P>The rears are coil overs , lowered as far as they will go , the car sits about 3" off the ground at the lowest point, so about a 2" drop. The tires are pirelli P Zero's , 255/40/17 rear , and 225/45's front<BR>The tire height is about .3-.5" off the factory 60 series tires<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>New Custom White face gauges 17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/jssig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Eric||01-29-2001||04:46 PM||||What is the Shannonville Motorsport Park?  Do you roadrace your Fiero?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Slammed Fiero||01-29-2001||05:09 PM||||Shannonville is located about an hour from kingston Ontario , 2 hours from toronto. Yeah I have been running my car on the track for about 4 years now as well as autocrossing , nothing too serious. <P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.shannonville.com/aeriel1.jpg"> <P>Fun track in my basically stock 86 GT I hit around 105mph on the long straights......<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>New Custom White face gauges 17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/jssig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Eric||01-29-2001||05:28 PM||||That's nice...  So you a member of a club or do you just pay to play every time you want to go fast?<P>I wish there was someplace around here where you could just have fun like that.  Most tracks won't let you on without all sorts of saftey equiptment unless you get a group togther and rent the track out.  Unfortunatly one of the best tracks ever made, Mid Ohio, is only about an hour away, and I don't think they'll let anyone on who's not a licensed race car driver.  I don't know if my Fiero is ready for a track like Mid Ohio, but my dad and I are building a Factory Five Cobra and it would be a real shame if there wasn't some place nearby to take it and wring it out (360 horsepower 2000 lbs, you do the math  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"> ).<P>There is a group of pretty serious autocrossers in my area.  I've taken my 88GT out several times only to be embarassed by some weird guys driving Miatas.  Next year I'll have my suspension rebuilt before I take it to the track.  Send those fruits home cryin' in their dinky little girly cars.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Slammed Fiero||01-29-2001||06:10 PM||||I belong to the St lawrence autoclub , a lot of our members run the one lap of america , 3 of them have won their class int he last 3 years...pretty serious guys.<P>We pay about $40 for 5 hours of lapping , We hold a lapping school in the spring which is around $90 for the day (8 til 6) plus you get the benifit of having a trained driver in the car with you giving you pointers. We have a novice , intermediate and pro group go out for 30 min sessions. After a day you usually need new front brake pads and have to flush the brake system (in a fiero. My last time there I ran our 87 Vette , after one day i had fried the alternator (notirous on c4 vettes) and boiled the brake fluid..I was smiling for a couple days.<P>The last time I ran the fiero was by far the most fun. A Vr6 corrado kept looking in his rearview but I was beside him , I out braked and cornered a 94 5.0ltr and passed a Neon RT on the long straight..great adrenaline rush...<P>We only allow passng on the straight section for most drivers. Guys who run the one lap , my dad ect..people who have been racing for a long time go out and get a little more serious...Funny to see sparks fly out the wheels of 928 porsche that trys to brake along side a 911 thats 1000lbs lighter.....<P><BR>all in all it's good fun. a fiero is a little hard to master since the trialing throttle oversteer. but with a little practice it can become quite entertaining. I have to say though for a 23 year old student it gets a litttle expensive to go to a lot of these events , 17" tires aren't cheap.....<P><BR>I urge everyone to take their fiero to a local autocross and test the limits of the car and your driving , it will make you a better driver. I wish they had autocrosses at fiero shows....<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||rogergarrison||01-29-2001||06:42 PM||||eric, you can run your car at Mid Ohio. Some SCCA clubs use the track for fun about once a month. You do have to have belts, helmet, fire extinquisher. Or you can enroll in one of the weekend driving schools, use your own car. At Powell Speedway on Powell Road on the north side between Sawmill and #23 the Mercedes Club rents the track for autocrossing one weekend I think in august. Its open to all makes on saturday, just Mercedes on sunday. I used to take my 560sl out there, that was a blast, even spun out twice.||||reg||1
Z||000009||JohnnyK||01-29-2001||07:02 PM||||Do they do any sort of stock car racing at this track? (Ontario). I've been looking for a place to get into it, and I can't really find anywhere except Barrie and Flamborough.. Guess I should get a car first, though.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Eric||01-29-2001||07:35 PM||||When can I sign up for the Powell Motor Speedway event, Roger?  I've never been on the track, but I seen it for the road dozens of times.  You guys must spend the most of the day weedwhackin' before the course is actually drivable.  Looks like a jungle sometimes.<P>I'll have to check into the Mid Ohio thing.  A lot of places don't let Cobras in because the single roll hoop "doesn't provide enough rollover protection".  It's the same at the drag strip.||||reg||1
